# Smoke check: the scenario

Import CoordinatorWire from "./coordinator_wire.lg".
Import LoadRules from "./load_rules.lg".
Import SmokeBuild from "./smoke_build.lg".
Import SmokeHttp from "./smoke_http.lg".

`factory coordinator smoke <base-url>` drives a running coordinator through the
whole worker protocol on the fixture problem `smoke:coordinator`
(`tests/fixtures/coordinator/smoke`, loaded with `coordinator load`): a lease
and its heartbeats, a recorded attempt, a stale repost refused, a known dead end
refused, an attempt resealed onto a head it did not see, a statement proposed and
reviewed twice until it is queued for the verifier, and the trail re-hashed
intact. It writes only to the fixture's trail, and it is meant for a development
or staging database, never the public one.

## A SmokeLog has:
    a lines, which is Seq of Text.
    a failures, which is Int.

## To smokeStep (log: SmokeLog, ok: Bool, what: Text) -> SmokeLog:
    Let mutable out be log.
    If ok:
        Push "ok      " + what to out's lines.
    Otherwise:
        Push "FAILED  " + what to out's lines.
        Set out's failures to out's failures + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
One attempt posted on a fresh lease of `kinds`; the log says whether it was
answered `expect`.

## To smokeAttempt (base: Text, log: SmokeLog, holder: Text, kinds: Text, verdict: Text, seed: Text, expect: Text) -> SmokeLog:
    Inspect smokeLease(base, holder, kinds, "smoke:coordinator"):
        When Err (e):
            Return smokeStep(log, false, holder + " leases a " + kinds + " unit: " + e).
        When Ok (g):
            Let mutable draft be none.
            If kinds is equal to "formalize" and verdict is equal to "verified":
                Set draft to smokeDraft().
            Let o be smokePost(base, smokeSubmission(g, holder, verdict, seed, g's trailSeq, g's trailHead, draft)).
            Let mutable ok be o's receipt's outcome is equal to expect.
            If expect is equal to "awaiting_verifier" and kinds is equal to "review":
                Set ok to o's status is equal to 201.
            Return smokeStep(log, ok, holder + " posts a " + verdict + " " + kinds + " attempt: answered {o's status} " + o's receipt's outcome).
    Return log.

## To coordinatorSmoke (base: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Let mutable log be a new SmokeLog.
    Let health be smokeCall("GET", base + "/api/v1/health", "").
    Set log to smokeStep(log, health's status is equal to 200, "the coordinator is healthy ({health's status})").
    Let seed be "{now()}".
    Inspect smokeLease(base, "smoke-a", "formalize", "smoke:coordinator"):
        When Err (e):
            Set log to smokeStep(log, false, "smoke-a leases the fixture problem: " + e).
        When Ok (g):
            Set log to smokeStep(log, smokeHeartbeat(base, g, "smoke-a", g's secret), "a heartbeat with the lease secret keeps it alive").
            Set log to smokeStep(log, smokeHeartbeat(base, g, "smoke-a", repeatText("0", 64)) is equal to false, "a heartbeat with a forged secret does not").
            Let body be smokeSubmission(g, "smoke-a", "rejected", seed + "-wall", g's trailSeq, g's trailHead, none).
            Let first be smokePost(base, body).
            Set log to smokeStep(log, first's status is equal to 201 and first's receipt's followUnit is not equal to "", "a rejected attempt is recorded and queues a retry").
            Let again be smokePost(base, body).
            Set log to smokeStep(log, again's status is equal to 409 and again's receipt's outcome is equal to "stale_lease", "the same attempt posted again is a stale lease").
            Set log to smokeResealed(base, log, g, seed).
            Set log to smokeAttempt(base, log, "smoke-c", "review", "verified", seed + "-review-c", "awaiting_verifier").
            Set log to smokeAttempt(base, log, "smoke-d", "review", "verified", seed + "-review-d", "awaiting_verifier").
    Let problem be smokeCall("GET", base + "/api/v1/problem?id=smoke:coordinator", "").
    Let check be textOfJson(jsonGet(jsonParse(problem's body), "trailCheck")).
    Set log to smokeStep(log, check is equal to "intact", "the fixture's trail re-hashes intact ({check})").
    If log's failures is greater than 0:
        Return a new Err with error join(log's lines, "\n") + "\n{log's failures} step(s) failed".
    Return a new Ok with value join(log's lines, "\n") + "\nevery step passed".

## Note
The retry, leased by another contributor: the failed approach again is a dead
end, and a statement built against the head the first lease saw is resealed
onto the newer head.

## To smokeResealed (base: Text, log: SmokeLog, stale: LeaseGrant, seed: Text) -> SmokeLog:
    Inspect smokeLease(base, "smoke-b", "formalize", "smoke:coordinator"):
        When Err (e):
            Return smokeStep(log, false, "smoke-b leases the retry: " + e).
        When Ok (g):
            Let wall be smokePost(base, smokeSubmission(g, "smoke-b", "rejected", seed + "-wall", g's trailSeq, g's trailHead, none)).
            Let mutable out be smokeStep(log, wall's status is equal to 409 and wall's receipt's outcome is equal to "dead_end", "the failed approach tried again is a dead end").
            Let o be smokePost(base, smokeSubmission(g, "smoke-b", "verified", seed + "-statement", stale's trailSeq, stale's trailHead, smokeDraft())).
            Return smokeStep(out, o's status is equal to 201 and o's receipt's resealed, "a statement built on an old head is resealed onto the new one ({o's status})").
    Return log.
